<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">light</ansi>

How well you can see where you are, and what it means in a fight.

Rooms are dark, dim, or lit, depending on the time of day, the weather,
whether you're indoors, and the light people carry. A torch, a lantern, or
the <ansi fg="command">floatinglight</ansi> spell lights your way. A companion's or ally's light in
your party lights you too.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Torches and lanterns</ansi>

- A <ansi fg="yellow">torch</ansi> is used up when you light it (<ansi fg="command">light torch</ansi>). It burns for about
  six game hours (fifteen minutes of real time) and can't be put out.
- A <ansi fg="yellow">lantern</ansi> lasts, but burns oil. Hold it in your off hand (<ansi fg="command">wear lantern</ansi>)
  and <ansi fg="command">light lantern</ansi>; it gives light while lit and burns an hour of oil each
  game hour. <ansi fg="command">douse lantern</ansi> puts it out and saves the oil. Put away in your
  pack, it goes out.
- A full lantern holds about a game day of oil (an hour of real time).
  When it runs dry it goes out. A <ansi fg="yellow">flask of lamp oil</ansi> fills it again:
  <ansi fg="command">fill lantern</ansi>.
- The markets of Dunmar and the Old Kings Road sell lanterns, torches and
  lamp oil (<ansi fg="command">help market</ansi>).
- Only you light a torch or lantern: a companion holding one gets no light
  from it. A companion's light spell still lights your party.
- Logged out with your lantern lit, it burns nothing while you are away.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Fighting in the dark</ansi>

- In <ansi fg="yellow">darkness</ansi>, every blow is 40% less likely to hit.
- In <ansi fg="yellow">dim</ansi> light, 10% less likely.
- A foe carrying a light is easier to see, and counts as no worse than dim.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">light</ansi>
  Show the light here, whether you carry one (and your lantern's oil), and
  your to-hit penalty.

  <ansi fg="command">light lantern</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">light torch</ansi>
  Light your held lantern, or a torch from your pack.

  <ansi fg="command">douse lantern</ansi>
  Put your lantern out, saving its oil.

  <ansi fg="command">fill lantern</ansi>
  Fill your lantern from a flask of lamp oil.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp gear</ansi>.
